# Candidate tables for the concrete 280-vertex Hall–Janko graph

Rows are order-three permutations, one generator for each candidate cyclic
subgroup. The breadth-first words and signed transitions use the exact ATLAS
left permutations. Fixed-point fingerprints separate rows and permutation
points. No assertion is inferred from the generator script: `Checks` verifies
these data in Lean's kernel and `Orbit` proves coverage.

Source: Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups*, 47.3 and 47.5, pp.261–263;
ATLAS J2G1-p100B0, with attribution retained in AtlasCarriers/source/.
